`Cmd/List.pm:194-208`. Four problems in one comparator:

| field | karr | kanban-md (`internal/board/sort.go`) |
|---|---|---|
| `status` | alphabetical (`backlog, review, todo`) | config order (`backlog, todo, review`) |
| `priority` | hardcoded critical->low | `cfg.PriorityIndex`, i.e. low->critical — **exactly reversed**, and karr ignores the config's `priorities` |
| `due` | `'' cmp` puts tasks without a date **first** | nil sorts **last** |
| unknown | `Can't locate object method "bogus" via package "App::karr::Task" at List.pm line 204` rc=1 | falls back to `id` |

The unknown-field case also means `$a->$field` calls an arbitrary method name
taken from user input — `--sort slug` and `--sort to_markdown` both execute. It
only fires with >= 2 tasks, since the comparator never runs on a 0/1-task board.

Fix: validate the sort field against a whitelist (exit 2 on anything else, per
ADR 0002), take status and priority order from the config, and sort missing due
dates last.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
